  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the average outcome (without weighting by probabilities) and counting how many outcomes are strictly greater than that average. Both lotteries have one outcome above the average (3000 > 2000 for A; 3000 > 1500 for B), so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention the average outcome or any comparison of outcomes above that average. Instead, the individual focuses on the 5% difference in probabilities and the preference for the higher sum (which is 4000 in B), and the neutrality of the worst case. This indicates that the individual did not apply the decision reason. The justification is based on sum size and risk perception, not on the number of outcomes above the average. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
